{
 "_comment": "LTX-2.3 TALKING HEAD WITH A CHOSEN VOICE: ID-LoRA (TalkVid-3K) + a ~5 s reference voice clip, through ComfyUI's native LTXVReferenceAudio. Flattened from ComfyUI's own template video_ltx2_3_id_lora by scripts/ui2api.py. The r/comfyui influencer recipe (2026-09): IC/ID-LoRA on LTX 2.3 with [VISUAL]: / [SPEECH]: / [SOUNDS]: sections. Measured 2026-09-17 by studio/_tools/id_lora_test.py (LTX_PLAYBOOK §97.1): it carries the VOICE - speaker similarity to the reference 0.816 against 0.58 without it, 3 of 3 seeds. The face is held by the start frame either way, and the words were spoken 100% with or without the tags. Not auditioned.",
 "_notes": [
  "Inputs: node 269 LoadImage = the start frame (16:9, the face large); node 276 LoadAudio = the reference voice, ~5 s of one speaker (the node's own tooltip: the training duration).",
  "Prompt: node sg1_319. The tags are [VISUAL]: [SPEECH]: [SOUNDS]: - SOUNDS plural, per the ID-LoRA model card; the Reddit comment that popularised this wrote [SOUND].",
  "The ID-LoRA was trained on LTX-2.3. It is a delta on 2.3 weights - workflow 70 loads it onto LTX-2.5, which is a different base (see §97).",
  "Two stages: half resolution, x2 latent upsampler, refine. Seeds: sg1_286 (stage 1), sg1_285 (stage 2).",
  "Identity guidance (sg1_349.identity_guidance_scale, default 3) runs an extra forward pass without the reference on every step - it is the voice's strength, and it costs time.",
  "Changes from the template: the three VAE links ui2api could not resolve are the checkpoint's VAE; the unused SolidMask is removed; 10 s -> 4.8 s (121 frames, 8n+1)."
 ],
